# handler/messaging/ is mid-split, and these two entries record where it got to
# rather than where it should end up:
#
#   messaging.rs was 2,395 lines. 1,674 of those were its test module, now
#   messaging/tests.rs — long, and legitimately so; the suite covers the
#   destroy/CleanupGuard coupling case by case.
#
#   messaging/mod.rs is 644, down from 721 after the pure decision helpers moved
#   to messaging/decisions.rs. It is still over the limit, and the reason is one
#   function: `send_message_inner` is ~530 lines carrying the whole send path —
#   interceptors, extension and streaming checks, id and metadata validation,
#   capacity admission, three-phase stale-token eviction, and task creation.
#   Splitting *that* is the remaining work, and it is a hot-path refactor rather
#   than a file move, so it is recorded here instead of being done badly under
#   time pressure.
#
# store/sqlite_store.rs became store/sqlite_store/ when the artifact journal was
# added — those entries are renamed, not new:
#
#   sqlite_store/mod.rs is 714, down from 1,529, after the two test modules and
#   the journal moved to their own files. What is left is the store itself, and
#   splitting `TaskStore`'s methods across files would separate `save` from the
#   `save_artifact_delta` that falls back to it — the coupling a reader most
#   needs to see in one place.
#
#   sqlite_store/tests.rs is 721, and is here for the same reason
#   messaging/tests.rs is: the content did not grow, it moved out of a file
#   already recorded. It is long because what it pins is broad — schema, CRUD,
#   listing, pagination, filters and concurrency, each against real SQLite —
#   and splitting it by feature would scatter the fixtures they share.
